Hi all,

I have three specimens with a large dataset of 3D landmarks (11,000 per specimen). Some landmarks are missing and I therefore need to estimate their position using estimate.missing before being able to perform a GPA with gpagen. It appears that there is a limitation of around 579 Landmarks. When I reduce the 3D array to 579 landmarks [1:579, 1:3, 1:3] I receive an output, but as soon as I increase the number of Landmarks above the 579 threshold, e.g.

[1:580, 1:3, 1:3], I receive the following error:

Error in gpagen(A[, , -spec.NA, PrinAxes = FALSE) :
  Coordinates array does not have proper dimensions

Is there a way to circumvent this limitation? Subdividing the specimens into smaller junks of 579 landmarks might skew the GPA and is thus not really an option.

I would be grateful for any help with my issue.

Many thanks in advance,

Ashleigh

